  "nl_text": "The database name is rschema_0463, and it contains three tables: Mall, Department, and Employee. The Mall table has four columns: Address, Contact_Number, Mall_ID, and Mall_Name. The Department table has eight columns: Contact_Number, Department_ID, Department_Name, Location_Distribution, Mall_ID, Manager_Employee_ID, Tenure, and Foreign keys to the Mall and Employee tables. The Employee table has seven columns: Department_ID, Emergency_Contact_Name, Emergency_Contact_Phone, Employee_ID, Name, Phone_Number, Position, and Salary. The Mall_ID and Manager_Employee_ID columns in the Department table are foreign keys that reference the Mall and Employee tables, respectively. The Department_ID column in the Employee table is a foreign key that references the Department table. The Mall, Department, and Employee tables all have primary keys, and the Department and Employee tables have foreign keys that reference each other.",
  "gold_question": "Business Requirements Description:\nGroup Company Business Operations Database System:\n1.Mall Management: The system records basic information for each mall, including mall ID, mall name, address, and contact number.\n2.Department Management: Each mall contains different departments. The system records information for each department, including department ID, department name, location distribution, and contact number.\n3.Employee Management: Each department hires multiple employees to handle daily affairs, and each employee can only belong to one department. The system records each employee’s information, including employee ID, name, position, phone number, and salary. Each department has a manager, and the system records the manager’s tenure.\n4.Emergency Contact Management: The system requires that each employee must and can only register one emergency contact’s name and phone number.",
  "input_json": "/data/RSchema_ExpResults4/Experiment2/schema2text_codellama13b/0463.json",
  "ddl": "-- Schema for database: rschema_0463\nCREATE TABLE `Mall` (\n  `Mall_ID` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `Mall_Name` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `Address` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `Contact_Number` varchar(15) NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`Mall_ID`)\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `Department` (\n  `Department_ID` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `Department_Name` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `Location_Distribution` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `Contact_Number` varchar(15) NOT NULL,\n  `Mall_ID` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `Manager_Employee_ID` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `Tenure` int(11) DEFAULT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`Department_ID`),\n  CONSTRAINT `department_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`Mall_ID`) REFERENCES `Mall` (`Mall_ID`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE,\n  CONSTRAINT `department_ibfk_2` FOREIGN KEY (`Manager_Employee_ID`) REFERENCES `Employee` (`Employee_ID`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `Employee` (\n  `Employee_ID` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `Name` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `Phone_Number` varchar(15) NOT NULL,\n  `Position` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `Salary` decimal(10,2) NOT NULL,\n  `Emergency_Contact_Name` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `Emergency_Contact_Phone` varchar(15) NOT NULL,\n  `Department_ID` int(11) DEFAULT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`Employee_ID`),\n  CONSTRAINT `employee_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`Department_ID`) REFERENCES `Department` (`Department_ID`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;",
